cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, dataset, or analysis pipeline,
  please cite both the companion paper and the Zenodo deposit
  using the metadata below.
title: >-
  Deep Learning Instance Segmentation for Wound Healing Assays --
  Annotated Image Dataset, Trained Models, and Analysis Pipeline
abstract: >-
  Companion repository for the manuscript "Deep Learning Instance
  Segmentation for Quantitative Analysis of Cell Migration in Wound
  Healing Assays: A Benchmark and Web-Accessible Tool", under major
  revision at Cytometry Part A (2026). Provides the complete
  pipeline: dataset assembly, training, evaluation, the statistical
  analysis (Pearson, Lin's concordance correlation, Bland-Altman,
  TOST) and the deployed web application. The associated deposit
  archives 1,363 annotated brightfield images (1,030 HUVEC and 333
  SKOV-3) partitioned over 246 acquisition units, 25 YOLO11
  detection runs (five configurations at five seeds each), five runs
  of a U-Net architectural comparator, and a supervised reference
  standard of 223 measured frames from which 97 paired observations
  across 45 acquisition series enter the agreement analysis.
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-03"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - MIT
license-url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21779854"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nykemariotto/scratch-assay-segmentation"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/nmariotto/Scratch-assay-segmentation"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20298129
    description: >-
      Zenodo concept DOI, which always resolves to the latest
      version of the deposit.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21779854
    description: >-
      Zenodo version DOI for v2.0.0, the version this study uses.
      It supersedes v1.0.0 (10.5281/zenodo.20298130) in full: the
      partition was redrawn over acquisition units, the models were
      retrained on it, and a supervised reference standard was
      built, so no count in v1.0.0 is comparable.
keywords:
  - instance segmentation
  - wound healing assay
  - scratch assay
  - HUVEC
  - SKOV-3
  - YOLO11
  - U-Net
  - brightfield microscopy
  - Segment Anything Model
  - deep learning
  - cell migration assays
  - observer agreement
  - reference standard
